    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Three angles of a pentagon are each $156^\\circ$ and the remaining angles are equal. Find the size of the two remaining angles.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$36^\\circ$ each.",
      "worked": "The pentagon angle sum is $540^\\circ$. The two equal remaining angles sum to $540^\\circ-3(156^\\circ)=72^\\circ$. Each is $\\frac{72^\\circ}{2}=36^\\circ$.",
